ntity\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Give the agent its own non-human identity. Keep it separate from the user who launched it and from unrelated agents. Show that permissions and revocation belong to that identity, even when a user starts the run.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Action records missing any of the six identity fields\",\n          \"owner\": \"A02\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Instance or tenant labels taken from what the model supplies\",\n          \"owner\": \"A04\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"A credential scoped to more operations, resources, or tenants than needed\",\n          \"owner\": \"B02\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Revocation delay from cached or self-contained tokens not measured\",\n          \"owner\": \"B04\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"gap\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml\",\n          \"line\": 19,\n          \"note\": \"Dedicated service account, SPIFFE id bound to it\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A01.1\",\n          \"check\": \"The agent runs under its own workload principal (service account, IAM role, SPIFFE ID, or agent ID) that no other service or unrelated agent uses.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find the agent's identity: pod `serviceAccountName`, IAM role, SPIFFE ID, or agent ID in IaC or deploy config. 2) Search other deployments, services, and agents in the repo for the same name or role. 3) Answer no if it is shared, `default`, the main backend's identity, or only a string label with no credential. Answer unknown if identity is assigned outside this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml:19\",\n          \"quote\": \"serviceAccountName: procurement-agent\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched the repo for other workloads using procurement-agent or default SA; only this deployment.\",\n          \"note\": \"Dedicated service account, SPIFFE id bound to it\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A01.2\",\n          \"check\": \"Tool and API clients get credentials from the agent's own principal, not from the launching user's forwarded token or session cookie.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find every place tool and API clients get a token or key. 2) Trace where each comes from: workload identity or token exchange, versus the incoming request's `Authorization` header or session cookie. 3) Check every client, not just the main one. 4) Answer no if any client forwards the user's token or cookie as-is, or uses a shared static key.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"app/identity.py:100\",\n          \"quote\": \"resp = await client.post(\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched for Authorization forwarding of the user JWT; authenticate() only validates it and tools use broker.token_for.\",\n          \"note\": \"Every client gets tokens through the STS exchange of the workload token\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A01.3\",\n          \"check\": \"When a user starts a run, the user is carried as a delegated subject (for example a token exchange with separate act and sub), while the agent keeps its own principal.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find the code that starts a run for a user. 2) Look for token exchange (RFC 8693, `subject_token`, `actor_token`, `act`/`sub` claims) or a separate delegated-subject field. 3) Check the agent's own principal is still the actor. 4) Answer no if the user's token is used directly or the user replaces the agent identity. Answer unknown if the exchange happens in an outside identity service.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"app/identity.py:95\",\n          \"quote\": \"key = (audience, scope, ident.tenant)\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Exchange carrie