{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FmsVPgKDDBx5unqmJiU5fM","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n \"item\": \"A04\",\n \"gate\": \"G1\",\n \"title\": \"Trustworthy attribution\",\n \"requirement\": \"Assign instance and tenant identity in the trusted execution layer. Don't accept labels the model supplies. Record the delegated subject \\u2014 the user or system whose authority is being used \\u2014 separately from the agent's identity. Test that the agent can't pose as another instance or tenant in requests or audit records. Test that trace context survives handoffs between async jobs. Treat trace IDs and caller-supplied labels only as a way to link records. They never prove identity or permission.\",\n \"rating\": \"gap\",\n \"confidence\": \"high\",\n \"evidence\": [\n  {\n   \"file\": \"app/tools/memory.py\",\n   \"line\": 112,\n   \"note\": \"memory_read schema lets the model fill the tenant\"\n  }\n ],\n \"red_flags_found\": [],\n \"violates\": [\n  \"Don't accept labels the model supplies.\"\n ],\n \"also_affects\": [\n  \"R05\",\n  \"B02\"\n ],\n \"summary\": \"memory_read lets the model fill the tenant field and the handler uses it unchanged.\",\n \"next_step\": \"Remove the business_unit argument and overwrite with the verified tenant.\",\n \"lead_role\": \"infrastructure\"\n}\nNOT COVERED [{\"problem\": \"Agent sharing the launching user's identity\", \"owner\": \"A01\"}, {\"problem\": \"Prompt a parent gave a sub-agent not recorded\", \"owner\": \"A06\"}, {\"problem\": \"Sub-agent authorized using an earlier actor's authority\", \"owner\": \"E08\"}, {\"problem\": \"Action records missing any of the six identity fields\", \"owner\": \"A02\"}]\n  CHK A04.1 no app/tools/memory.py:112 | None | Tenant and instance identity are set by the harness or platform from verified context, never from model-produced text or tool arguments.\n  CHK A04.2 no app/tools/memory.py:44 | None | Tenant or instance labels in tool arguments or agent-controlled headers are rejected or overwritten with the verified values before they are used or l\n{\n \"item\": \"A05\",\n \"gate\": \"G1\",\n \"title\": \"Operational lookup\",\n \"requirement\": \"Start from one suspicious action. Find the team responsible, the current operator, the deployment manifest, and the live instance. Show that you can contain the right instance or agent type without cutting off the launching user's other access.\",\n \"rating\": \"gap\",\n \"confidence\": \"low\",\n \"evidence\": [],\n \"red_flags_found\": [\n  \"app/killswitch.py:19, migrations/001_init.sql:96 The only containment control is the halt flag, scoped to the whole fleet or one tenant. There is no per-instance or per-agent-type halt or revoke. The check also runs only when a run starts (README:58), so it cannot stop a live instance. The tenant scope stops every agent instance in that business unit, not the one suspicious instance or type.\"\n ],\n \"violates\": [\n  \"contain the right instance or agent type\"\n ],\n \"also_affects\": [],\n \"summary\": \"Audit rows carry type and instance ids, but manifest lookup, on-call mapping and per-instance containment are not shown.\",\n \"next_step\": \"Show the manifest registry, on-call mapping and a per-instance scale-down or revoke control.\",\n \"lead_role\": \"operations\",\n \"challenge\": {\n  \"verdict\": \"failed\",\n  \"note\": \"Containment is limited to fleet-wide or tenant-wide halt flags checked at run start, so a single instance or agent type cannot be contained; manifest-store lookup and on-call ownership are not in the repo.\"\n }\n}\nNOT COVERED [{\"problem\": \"Stop doesn't halt running work or open tool streams within a set time\", \"owner\": \"R11\"}, {\"problem\": \"No drill for a compromised shared tool or agent type\", \"owner\": \"E12\"}, {\"problem\": \"Action records missing any of the six identity fields\", \"owner\": \"A02\"}]\n  CHK A05.1 unknown  | None | Each audit record carries the agent-type-id and agent-instance-id, which resolve to a stored deployment manifest and a live instance.\n  CHK A05.2 unknown  | None | An ownership record in code or config maps each agent type to a responsible team and a current operator or on-call rotation.\n  CHK A05.3 no app/killswitch.py:19, migrations/001_init.sql:96 | None | A containment control can disable a single instance or a single agent type (for example revoke its principal or scale it to zero) without touching the\n{\n \"item\": \"B02\",\n \"gate\": \"G1\",\n \"title\": \"Least-privilege access\",\n \"requirement\": \"Limit credentials to named operations and resources, including tenant boundaries. Test that an allowed read works. Test that an out-of-scope write, an admin action, and a request for another tenant's data all fail. Limit each token to its intended audience, so other services reject it. Remove wildcard permissions and permissions inherited from people.\",\n \"rating\": \"gap\",\n \"confidence\": \"high\",\n \"evidence\": [\n  {\n   \"file\": \"app/tools/memory.py\",\n   \"line\": 44,\n   \"note\": \"memory_read takes the tenant from a model-filled argument; DB login is shared with no row-level security\"\n  }\n ],\n \"red_flags_found\": [],\n \"violates\": [\n  \"a request for another tenant's data all fail\"\n ],\n \"also_affects\": [\n  \"R05\",\n  \"A04\"\n ],\n \"summary\": \"memory_read lets the model pick another business unit, and the database login is shared with no row-level security.\",\n \"next_step\": \"Ignore the business_unit argument and enforce tenant in the data layer.\",\n \"lead_role\": \"infrastructure\"\n}\nNOT COVERED [{\"problem\": \"A retrieval search or cache not filtered by the requesting tenant or user\", \"owner\": \"R04\"}, {\"problem\": \"Long-lived or static secrets that never expire or rotate\", \"owner\": \"B03\"}, {\"problem\": \"Revocation delay from cached or self-contained tokens\", \"owner\": \"B04\"}, {\"problem\": \"A sub-agent getting powers beyond its task, or a parent escalating through a peer\", \"owner\": \"E08\"}, {\"problem\": \"Memory readable across tenants or tasks\", \"owner\": \"R05\"}]\n  CHK B02.1 unknown  | None | The agent's IAM policy or role names specific actions and resources, with no `*` action or resource and no owner, editor, or cluster-admin role.\n  CHK B02.2 no app/tools/memory.py:44 | None | Tenant scope is enforced in the credential or the data layer (token claim, row-level security, or per-tenant account), not by the prompt or by code th\n  CHK B02.3 unknown  | None | Tokens are issued with a set audience, and receiving services reject tokens whose audience does not match.\n{\n \"item\": \"B04\",\n \"gate\": \"G1\",\n \"title\": \"Independent revocation\",\n \"requirement\": \"Show that an operator can cut off this agent's access without cutting off the user who launched it. The agent must not need to cooperate. Set and measure the longest time before the cutoff takes effect. Count cached tokens, self-contained tokens, and open sessions. A trusted enforcement point must block later calls within a time limit that fits the potential harm. Revoking only the refresh token is not enough. If tokens live longer than that limit, push the revocation to each service (for example, with OpenID CAEP session-revoked events) or make the tokens shorter-lived.\",\n \"rating\": \"gap\",\n \"confidence\": \"low\",\n \"evidence\": [],\n \"red_flags_found\": [\n  \"app/loop.py:127 The only stop control is a DB flag checked inside agent code, once at run start. It is not a trusted enforcement point outside the agent, and a running agent is never re-checked.\",\n  \"app/identity.py:97 Cached access tokens are reused until expiry with no revocation check. The access-token lifetime (expires_in) is set by the STS and is not stated in the repo. No maximum revocation time is stated, and no CAEP or introspection exists. The halt flag is only read at run start, so open runs continue.\"\n ],\n \"violates\": [\n  \"A truste